s5: expressing every named canonical exponent as max(K, e + I)
window: binades -40..40

Q1: the design's named shapes in the two-integer form
   ok  fixed point, f == -F, F=8              K=-8      I=-1000   -> constant
   ok  fixed point, f == -F, F=0              K=0       I=-1000   -> constant
   ok  float, p=24, f(e)=e-23                 K=-10000  I=-23     -> slope one
   ok  float, p=53, f(e)=e-52                 K=-10000  I=-52     -> slope one
   ok  gradual underflow, p=24, emin=-14      K=-37     I=-23     -> knee
   ok  gradual underflow, p=11, emin=-14      K=-24     I=-10     -> knee
   -> 6/6

Q2/Q3: closure over a pool of 81 grids, 6561 ordered pairs
   meet (pointwise max) stays in the family : 6561/6561
   the closed form max(max(K1,K2), e+max(I1,I2)) holds : True
   join (pointwise min) stays in the family : 3969/6561
   join leaves the family                   : 2592/6561

Q4: what the join lands in, for the two cases that differ

   A. join of a pure fixed shape (f == -8) and a pure float (f == e-23)
      slope runs: [(1, 55), (0, 25)]
      in the family max(K, e+I)? False
      slope one at the bottom then slope zero above, which is 08:436-440's
      mirror shape. It is min(K, e+I), one flip of the same two integers.

   B. join of two knees, (-12, -10) and (-10, -12)
      slope runs: [(0, 38), (1, 2), (0, 2), (1, 38)]
      in the family max(K, e+I)? False
      four segments, so it is not the mirror shape either. The join of two
      knees is strictly worse than the join 08 measured, and this is the
      case 08 did not have because its pool's join question was asked
      across kinds rather than within the knee family.

Reading:
  The knee needs two integers, not a list. The design's whole admitted set is
  the two-integer form, so the enumeration collision 08:392-396 names does not
  arise for the shapes the design actually has.
  Meet-closure is an algebraic identity on those two integers rather than a
  survey result, and non-closure under the join is the same identity failing
  in the other direction. 08 measured both; this says why.
  A design wanting the join total needs at least min-of-max-of-affine, and the
  segment count grows with each join, which is where the function-space
  question actually starts. Refusing the join keeps the shape at two integers.
